Given first term (a), common ratio (r) and a integer n of the Geometric Progression series, the task is to print the n terms of the series.Examples:

Input : a = 2 r = 2, n = 4Output : 2 4 8 16Approach : 

We know the Geometric Progression series is like = 2, 4, 8, 16, 32 ....... In this series 2 is the starting term of the series . Common ratio = 4 / 2 = 2 (ratio common in the series). so we can write the series as :t1 = a1 t2 = a1 * r(2-1) t3 = a1 * r(3-1) t4 = a1 * r(4-1) . . . . tN = a1 * r(n-1)  

To print the Geometric Progression series we use the simple formula . 

TN = a1 * r(n-1)

            CPP

    // CPP program to print GP.
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

void printGP(int a, int r, int n)
{
    int curr_term;
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        curr_term = a * pow(r, i);
        cout << curr_term << " ";
    }
}

// Driver code
int main()
{
    int a = 2; // starting number
    int r = 3; // Common ratio
    int n = 5; // N th term to be find
    printGP(a, r, n);
    return 0;
}


